.TH GETITIMER 2 "March 2026" "Substrate" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
getitimer \- read a process interval timer
.SH LIBRARY
Substrate libc
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <sys/time.h>

int getitimer(int which, struct itimerval *curr_value);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR getitimer ()
returns the current state of one of the calling process's interval timers in
.IR curr_value .
The
.I which
argument selects one of:
.TP
.B ITIMER_REAL
Decrements in wall-clock time and delivers
.B SIGALRM
on expiry.
.TP
.B ITIMER_VIRTUAL
Decrements only while the process is executing in user mode and delivers
.B SIGVTALRM
on expiry.
.TP
.B ITIMER_PROF
Decrements while the process is executing and delivers
.B SIGPROF
on expiry.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success,
.BR getitimer ()
returns 0.
On error, it returns -1 and sets
.BR errno .
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
.I which
is not a supported interval timer.
.TP
.B EFAULT
.I curr_value
does not reference writable user memory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR alarm (2),
.BR setitimer (2),
.BR signal (2)
